extends ../layout/page.pug

block title
  | Nav-bar search — download UI mockups · lilnas

//-
  The one entry point for both jobs — paste a link, or search a title. This
  page is a reference rather than a screen: where the field lives at each
  width, every state it can be in, then the two flows end to end.

//- A card sized to hold one field in isolation.
mixin stateCard
  div(class='max-w-[400px] rounded-lg border border-line bg-bg-sunk p-[18px]')&attributes(attributes)
    block

//-
  Numbered step in a flow: number, the framed field (the mixin's block), then
  the explanation. `desc` is a parameter rather than a second block because a
  Pug mixin only gets one.
mixin flowstep(num, title, desc)
  div(class='flex items-start gap-[18px]')&attributes(attributes)
    span(
      class='mt-0.5 grid h-[26px] w-[26px] shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-surface-3 font-mono text-mono-sm font-semibold text-ink-2'
    )= num
    div(class='w-[280px] shrink-0')
      block
    div(class='min-w-0 flex-1 pt-[5px]')
      p(class='text-h3')= title
      p(class='text-sm text-ink-3')= desc

//- What happens between two steps, and on what motion.
mixin flowConnector
  div(class='my-2.5 ml-[13px] flex items-center gap-[9px]')&attributes(attributes)
    +icon('arrow')(class='h-3 w-3 shrink-0 rotate-90 text-ink-4')
    span(class='font-mono text-mono-sm text-uv-hi')
      block

block content
  +mockHead({ eyebrow: 'lilnas · download', title: 'Nav-bar search' })
    p(class='max-w-[62ch] text-sm text-ink-3')
      | The single entry point for both jobs — paste a video link, or search for a movie or show — reachable
      | from the nav bar on every page except #[code(class='font-mono text-mono-sm') search.html], whose own
      | hero already IS the search. On desktop it sits inline in the bar; on mobile it collapses to an icon and
      | expands to take over the bar on tap. It classifies what's typed and branches automatically: once there's
      | something to act on, a compact button appears right in the pill — Download for a detected link, Search
      | for a title query of 2+ characters — so pressing Enter and clicking the button do the same thing.
      | Below: where it lives in the bar at each width, then every state the field itself can be in, then the
      | full sequence for both branches, up to the redirect. What each destination looks like lives in that
      | page's own file, not here.

  //-
    Where it lives — the bar itself, at both widths. Distinct from the states
    catalog below: this is about reaching the field at all, not what it does
    once visible.
  section(class='mb-14' id='chrome')
    h2(class='mb-1.5 text-[22px] leading-[1.25] font-[650] tracking-[-0.015em]') In the app bar: desktop vs. mobile
    p(class='mb-6 max-w-[62ch] text-sm text-ink-3')
      | Desktop has room for the field inline, next to the doorplate. Mobile doesn't — competing against the
      | doorplate, the live-download chip, and the account avatar in one row, the field loses and collapses to
      | an icon, expanding to take over the bar on tap.

    div(class='vp-scope')
      +viewportToggle('viewport')(class='mb-7' role='radiogroup' aria-label='Viewport')

      +viewportPanel('desktop')
        +frameLabel Inline, always
        +appFrame('desktop')
          +navBar('desktop', { placeholder: 'Search or paste a link…', tall: true })
          +appBody('desktop')
            p(class='text-sm text-ink-3')
              | Never leaves the bar — no tap needed to reach it. Same field, same states as "One field, every
              | state" below.

      +viewportPanel('mobile')
        +frameLabel Collapsed, at rest
        +appFrame('mobile')
          +appBar('mobile')
            +doorplate('Download')(href='https://lilnas.io')
            span(class='flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1.5')
              +chip({ tone: 'ok' })
                +dot('live')
                | 2
              +btn({ variant: 'ghost', icon: 'search' })(class='h-[30px] w-[30px] p-0' aria-label='Search')
              +accountLink('JA')
          +appBody('mobile')
            p(class='text-sm text-ink-3')
              | The doorplate, live status, and account all need the row — the field loses that fight, so it's
              | an icon until tapped. Every other mockup's mobile frame shows this exact resting state.

        +frameLabel()(class='mt-3') Expanded, on tap
        +appFrame('mobile')
          +appBar('mobile')
            +btn({ variant: 'ghost', icon: 'x' })(class='h-[30px] w-[30px] shrink-0 p-0' aria-label='Close search')
            +navsearch({ placeholder: 'Search or paste a link…', tall: true })
          +appBody('mobile')
            p(class='text-sm text-ink-3')
              | Takes over the bar full-width — doorplate, status, and avatar step aside until it closes. Same
              | field, same states as below; closing it, or a redirect firing, hands the bar back.

  //-
    States catalog — a reference: every state in isolation. They're mutually
    exclusive, so each gets its own card rather than being stacked into one
    scroll.
  section(id='states')
    h2(class='mb-1.5 text-[22px] leading-[1.25] font-[650] tracking-[-0.015em]') One field, every state
    p(class='mb-2 max-w-[62ch] text-sm text-ink-3')
      | Grouped by what caused it, not by how it looks. The field is always in exactly one of these.

    div(class='grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr))] gap-8')
      div(class='min-w-0')
        p(class='mb-2.5 text-h3' id='state-idle') Idle
        p(class='mb-[14px] text-sm text-ink-3')
          | Nothing typed yet. Identical whether what comes next turns out to be a link or a title.
        +stateCard
          +navsearch({ placeholder: 'Search or paste a link…', tall: true })

      div(class='min-w-0')
        p(class='mb-2.5 text-h3' id='state-link') A link is detected
        p(class='mb-[14px] text-sm text-ink-3')
          | Classification is instant and client-side — no network round-trip, so no separate "resolving"
          | state. The icon swaps and a compact Download button appears right in the pill.
        +stateCard
          +navsearch({ tall: true, ready: true, value: 'youtube.com/watch?v=7f2k9dQ', icon: 'download' })
            +navsearchGo('Download')

      div(class='min-w-0')
        p(class='mb-2.5 text-h3' id='state-query') A title query is ready
        p(class='mb-[14px] text-sm text-ink-3')
          | Anything that isn't a link, once it clears 2+ characters — the same threshold §3's search uses.
          | Same treatment as a detected link: the icon tints and a compact Search button appears.
        +stateCard
          +navsearch({ tall: true, ready: true, value: 'the office' })
            +navsearchGo('Search')

  //-
    Full flow — the happy-path narrative, connected in order. Failure states
    live in the catalog above and on video-detail.html, not here.
  section(class='mt-14 border-t border-line-soft pt-[30px]' id='flow')
    h2(class='mb-1.5 text-[22px] leading-[1.25] font-[650] tracking-[-0.015em]') Full flow, start to finish
    p(class='mb-5 max-w-[62ch] text-sm text-ink-3')
      | Both branches start in the exact same nav-bar field — paste a link for a video, or type a title for a
      | movie or show. From there they diverge: a video redirects straight to its own detail page, where the
      | download starts; a title search redirects to the search results page. Nothing downloads, and no
      | results render, inside the field itself.

    div(class='my-6 mb-10 rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface px-4 py-[14px]')
      p(class='text-sm text-ink-3')
        | Captions cite #[code(class='font-mono text-mono-sm') docs/designs/motion.md]. Two motions only:
        | #[b(class='text-ink') spring] — the user pressed or dragged something (120ms) — and
        | #[b(class='text-ink') ease] — the system reacting to data or a route (200–380ms). These are
        | motion.md's #[code(class='font-mono text-mono-sm') --ease-uv] /
        | #[code(class='font-mono text-mono-sm') --ease-spring], which this build exposes as the
        | #[code(class='font-mono text-mono-sm') ease-uv] and #[code(class='font-mono text-mono-sm') ease-spring]
        | Tailwind utilities.

    +flowstep('0', 'At rest', 'Both branches start here, in the nav bar — on every page, not just one. See "Idle" above.')
      +stateCard()(class='max-w-[320px]')
        +navsearch({ placeholder: 'Search or paste a link…', tall: true })

    +flowConnector
      | classifies instantly, client-side — a link swaps the icon and shows Download; anything else is a
      | title, and shows Search once it's 2+ characters

    div(class='mt-[30px] mb-[18px]')
      p(class='mb-1 font-mono text-label tracking-[0.11em] uppercase text-uv') Branch A
      h3(class='text-h3') Fetch a video

    +flowstep('1', 'Typing', 'Still just text — search icon, no button yet. Not host-shaped, so not a link. Yet.')
      +stateCard()(class='max-w-[320px]')
        +navsearch({ tall: true, value: 'youtub' })

    +flowConnector
      | no network round-trip — classification is a client-side check, not a fetch

    +flowstep('2', 'Link detected', 'Icon swaps, button appears — no dropdown, no preview card. See "A link is detected" above.')
      +stateCard()(class='max-w-[400px]')
        +navsearch({ tall: true, ready: true, value: 'youtube.com/watch?v=7f2k9dQ', icon: 'download' })(class='reveal')
          +navsearchGo('Download')

    +flowConnector
      | press Download: 120ms spring, scale(0.96) → route change: 380ms rise

    +note('download')(class='reveal')
      b(class='text-ink') Redirects to the video's detail page.
      |  Extraction and the download both start the moment it loads — no separate preview-before-committing
      | step. If yt-dlp doesn't recognize the link after all, that page shows a "not recognized" state instead
      | of progress. See #[a(class='text-ink underline' href='video-detail.html') video-detail.html].

    div(class='mt-11 border-t border-line-soft pt-[26px] pb-[18px]')
      p(class='mb-1 font-mono text-label tracking-[0.11em] uppercase text-uv') Branch B
      h3(class='text-h3') Find a movie or show

    +flowstep('1', 'Typing', 'Same field as Branch A, reachable from every page. Under 2 characters — still just text, no button yet.')
      +stateCard()(class='max-w-[320px]')
        +navsearch({ tall: true, value: 't' })

    +flowConnector
      | same client-side check as the link branch — counting length instead of parsing a host

    +flowstep('2', 'Query ready', '2+ characters — icon tints, a compact Search button appears. Pressing Enter does the same thing as clicking it. See "A title query is ready" above.')
      +stateCard()(class='max-w-[400px]')
        +navsearch({ tall: true, ready: true, value: 'the office' })(class='reveal')
          +navsearchGo('Search')

    +flowConnector
      | press Enter or click Search: 120ms spring on the button → route change: 380ms rise

    +note('search')(class='reveal')
      b(class='text-ink') Redirects to the search page.
      |  Results are already loading by the time the route lands —
      | #[code(class='font-mono text-mono-sm') search.html] owns the results list, filters, and sort from
      | there. See #[a(class='text-ink underline' href='search.html') search.html].

    +card()(class='mt-10')
      div(class='flex items-center gap-2.5')
        +dot('live')
        p(class='text-sm')
          | A download shows up on
          | #[a(class='text-uv-hi underline' href='downloads-activity.html') downloads-activity.html] the
          | instant it starts — immediately for Branch A, or once a result's picked and Download's pressed for
          | Branch B.
